[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How it was verified
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * C reference: `cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && cmake --build .`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   → `c_src/build/driver`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Rust: `cd translation && cargo build --release` → `translation/target/release/driver`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `translation/tests/differential.rs` spawns **both binaries** as subprocesses
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   with identical stdin and asserts stdout, stderr and exit status (exit code
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *and* terminating signal) are byte-for-byte equal. Nothing is loaded as a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   library.
